 managed service named 'inventory-worker' on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An OpenRC init script /etc/init.d/inventory-worker was created running a persistent shell loop; rc-service start succeeded, the service reported 'started', and process inspection showed the worker actively producing incrementing snapshot/log entries over a >12s observation window, confirming long-running behavior under OpenRC management.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-659fa906392f48df\",\"cmd-3766d8d3c0274200\",\"cmd-643fe432683645fd\"]},{\"id\":\"confinement-writes\",\"requirement\":\"Confine the service so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Inside the bwrap sandbox (root bind-mounted read-only, /var/lib/inventory bind-mounted read-write), a write attempt to /root failed with Permission denied, a write attempt to /etc failed with Read-only file system, and a write to /var/lib/inventory succeeded. This directly demonstrates the required write confinement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-18083a67f47d4147\"]},{\"id\":\"no-new-privs\",\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"NoNewPrivs:1 was observed both in a manual sandboxed shell test and directly in /proc/<pid>/status of the live, running service process, confirming the no-new-privileges constraint is enforced for the actual deployed service, not just a manual test.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-18083a67f47d4147\",\"cmd-643fe432683645fd\"]},{\"id\":\"unprivileged-execution\",\"requirement\":\"Worker runs unprivileged (supporting the confinement requirement)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A dedicated uid/gid 1001 'inventory' user was created and the live service process was confirmed running as uid/gid 1001 via /proc/<pid>/status, not as root.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-764a96fd707f4683\",\"cmd-643fe432683645fd\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Command trace reviewed chronologically. Diagnost